ssbook><name>KOMINE, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A synthetic quartz glass optical member to be used together with a light having a specific wave length of 250 nm or less which has a difference between the maximum and the minimum values of transmissivity [%/cm] per 1 cm of thickness of such a light in a given direction in a plane perpendicular to the ray axis of the light of 2.0 %/cm or less.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un élément optique en verre de quartz synthétique utilisé avec une lumière ayant une longueur d'onde spécifique de 250 nm ou moins, présentant une différence entre les valeurs maximum et minimum de transmissivité (%/cm) pour un centimètre d'épaisseur de cette lumière, dans un sens donné dans un plan perpendiculaire à l'axe de rayon de la lumière de 2,0 %/cm ou moins.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>